<article class="env-example" id="0GB6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GB6">Example <span data-tag="0GB6">87.12.2</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a weakly admissible topological ring. In this case we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{Spf}(A)_{red} = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A/\mathfrak a)  \]
</div>
  <p> where $\mathfrak a \subset A$ is the ideal of topologically nilpotent elements. Namely, $\mathfrak a$ is a radical ideal (Lemma <a href="/tag/0AMW" data-tag="0AMW">87.4.10</a>) which is open because $A$ is weakly admissible. </p>
</article>